From d32a79ac47729fac3941daea9029ff5694bc83b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anusha Srivatsa <asrivats@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:03:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] nvk: add indexed indirect count draw support for
 pre-Turing

Extend the pre-Turing indirect count draw path to handle the indexed
variant. The indexed path uses VkDrawIndexedIndirectCommand which has
5 dwords (vertex count, instance count, first index, vertex offset,
first instance) compared to 4 for the non-indexed command.

Add NVK_MME_SCRATCH_DRAW_TOTAL to the scratch registers to preserve
the original maxDrawCount across the draw loop, since the MME needs
it after clamping to drain unused FIFO entries for draws beyond the
actual count. The non-indexed path could keep this in a register, but
the indexed path has higher register pressure due to the additional
draw parameter.

Signed-off-by: Anusha Srivatsa <asrivats@redhat.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_draw.c | 127 ++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_mme.h      |   1 +
 2 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)

